<decision #track.add-real-tui-workflow-human-journey-e2e.network-fixture apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" } (
  <question ?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DH>
  The scenario says “from a network hot-topic portal”; should normal CI depend on a mutable public portal?
  </?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DH>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DJ>
    Use a real but deterministic network portal in the automated TUI E2E.
    </?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DJ>
    <decision-text ?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DK>
    Use an in-process deterministic HTTP portal for the required E2E test. It is a real network boundary, while public live-provider smoke remains optional evidence rather than a blocking CI baseline.
    </?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DK>
    <rationale ?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DM>
    The test must distinguish network execution from a fabricated report, but public content, availability and rate limits are not deterministic product contracts.
    </?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DM>
    <evidence ?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DN>
    The user requested a network hot-topic portal proposition; existing terminal E2E tests inject deterministic providers and isolated runtime state.
    </?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DN>
  )>
)>

<decision #track.add-real-tui-workflow-human-journey-e2e.confirmation-shape apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" } (
  <question ?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DP>
  How is human approval represented in this conversational acceptance test?
  </?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DP>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DQ>
    Confirm publication and execution in separate natural-language TUI turns.
    </?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DQ>
    <decision-text ?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DR>
    Use separate ordinary-language follow-up turns for publication confirmation and execution confirmation. The adapter must emit independent `publish` and `execute` authorizations, and production gates must enforce both.
    </?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DR>
    <rationale ?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DS>
    This matches the human conversation product contract and proves that publication never implies execution.
    </?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DS>
    <evidence ?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DT>
    The existing workflow journey contract defines independent publication and execution authorization states.
    </?01M05F1PRR31S1MK4K6C1SX3DT>
  )>
)>
